---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Advertising Disclosure"
  description="How NoCharge runs one labeled, responsive Google AdSense banner with Google Privacy & messaging consent, and how to report a problematic ad."
  path="/advertising/"
  showAds={false}
>
  <article class="trust-page prose">
    <Breadcrumbs items={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'Advertising Disclosure' }]} />
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Advertising Disclosure</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">How advertising and affiliate links work on NoCharge.</h1>
      <p class="lede">One labeled banner, clearly marked Amazon affiliate links, and no commercial links in gameplay.</p>
      <p class="trust-page__date">Last updated: August 21, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-relationship">
      <h2 id="ads-relationship">Google AdSense banner relationship</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge displays exactly one manual, responsive Google AdSense banner near the bottom of eligible pages,
        before the footer. The banner is clearly labeled &ldquo;Advertisement&rdquo; and is third-party advertising
        supplied through Google AdSense, not NoCharge editorial content. NoCharge does not run Google Auto ads and
        does not add more than one banner to a page.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-consent">
      <h2 id="ads-consent">Your advertising choice</h2>
      <p>
        Google Privacy &amp; messaging is the advertising consent platform. Where applicable, Google shows its own
        consent message before advertising is served, and the official AdSense tag follows the choice recorded
        there. NoCharge does not keep its own advertising consent toggle and does not translate any older site
        preference into Google&rsquo;s consent system.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can review or revoke your Google advertising choices at any time with the Privacy and cookie settings
        control in the footer or on the <a href="/privacy/">Privacy page</a>. It reopens Google&rsquo;s consent message.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-data">
      <h2 id="ads-data">Data Google may process</h2>
      <p>
        When a banner loads, your browser connects directly to Google. Google may use cookies or similar storage
        and may process data such as your IP address, browser and device details, page context, consent signals,
        measurement data, and information about ad interactions. See Google&rsquo;s
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and
        <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites">How Google uses information from sites that use Google services</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-labeling">
      <h2 id="ads-labeling">Labels, external destinations, and endorsement</h2>
      <p>
        The banner is identified as an advertisement. An advertisement or external link does not mean NoCharge
        endorses, verifies, or guarantees the destination, offer, product, service, safety, availability, or claims
        made there. Use your own judgment and review an external site&rsquo;s terms and privacy information before
        interacting with it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="affiliate-relationship">
      <h2 id="affiliate-relationship">Amazon affiliate links in Quiet Setup</h2>
      <p>NoCharge may publish clearly marked Amazon affiliate links in <a href="/setup/">Quiet Setup</a> and may earn commissions from qualifying purchases. <strong>As an Amazon Associate I earn from qualifying purchases.</strong> Page-level disclosure appears before the first paid link, and every paid link identifies Amazon and the paid relationship.</p>
      <p>Amazon links take visitors directly to Amazon. Amazon controls its own site, checkout, cookies, and privacy practices. NoCharge does not know a visitor&rsquo;s complete Amazon order details. No purchase is required to use NoCharge or play any game, and affiliate relationships do not influence scores, progression, game access, or game content.</p>
      <p>Quiet Setup recommendations use a documented editorial method and show their evidence level. Initial articles use editorial research, name limitations, consider no-purchase alternatives, and remain useful without affiliate links.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-isolation">
      <h2 id="ads-isolation">No ads over active gameplay</h2>
      <p>
        NoCharge does not place advertising over an active game viewport or inside game controls. On game pages the
        banner sits after the game details and related content, at least 150 pixels below the interactive game area,
        and it is never sticky or floating. Shared full-screen or immersive game mode contains only the game viewport
        and its controls. NoCharge does not run interstitials, anchors, popups, popunders, Smartlink fallbacks,
        automatic ad refreshes, or automatic top-level redirects to an advertiser destination.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="ads-report">
      <h2 id="ads-report">Report a problematic advertisement</h2>
      <p>
        If you see an advertisement or advertising destination that appears harmful, misleading, inappropriate, or
        broken, email <a href="mailto:hello@nocharge.net">hello@nocharge.net</a>. If possible, include the page
        where it appeared, the approximate date and time, and a description or screenshot. Do not send sensitive
        personal information. Reports help us review the placement, but NoCharge cannot guarantee Google&rsquo;s
        response or content removal.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .trust-page {
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.15rem;
    max-width: 48rem;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .trust-page > header {
    padding: 0.75rem 0 1.25rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line);
  }

  .trust-page__date {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
  }

  .trust-page section {
    padding-top: 0.25rem;
  }

  .trust-page section + section {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--line);
  }
</style>
